{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #102: declared status 'open'. Formalized: no. Let $c>0$ and $h_c(n)$ be such that for any $n$ points in $\\mathbb{R}^2$ such that there are $\\geq cn^2$ lines each containing more than three points, there must be some line containing $h_c(n)$ many points. Estimate $h_c(n)$. Is it true that, for fixed $c>0$, we have $h_c(n)\\to \\infty$? Current best: It is easy to see that $h_c(n) \\ll_c n^{1/2}$, and Erd\\H{o}s at one point \\cite{Er95} suggested that perhaps a similar lower bound $h_c(n)\\gg_c n^{1/2}$ holds. Prize: no. Tags: geometry."},"claim_id":"vcl_94047a42ebb8e1f747dcbb4272c84083cc2caebb7d79e3d6020f0399f53ea85b","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:102","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_ea9de85dbae7be5d","object_root":"sha256:168c75303625503cd48023b401e5df8d6088dc7b9c44abf99bb5c252902e0851","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:102"}],"relations":[],"revision":1,"sc